# Writing thesis Markdown

Full specification: `docs/llm-format/README.md` (ru) / `docs/llm-format/README.en.md` (en).
Output Markdown only; the sole HTML allowed is the `<!-- @suppress -->`
directive.

## Structure

- One logical section per file under the profile's `markdown_dir`; the build
  order is `markdown_files` in `config.yaml`. A new file is invisible until
  listed there.
- `_bundle.md` is generated by `merge` and deleted afterwards — never edit,
  reference or commit it.
- Headings: `# 1 Название`, `## 1.1 Подраздел`, no period after the number.
  Structural sections keep their canonical Russian caps names
  (`# ВВЕДЕНИЕ`, `# СПИСОК ИСПОЛЬЗОВАННЫХ ИСТОЧНИКОВ`, `# ПРИЛОЖЕНИЕ А`).
  Appendix letters skip I, O and Ё З Й О Ч Ь Ъ.

## Numbered objects always use a key

```markdown
![схема](pipeline.png)
Рисунок {pipeline} - Конвейер обработки

Таблица {req} - Требования
| Параметр | Значение |
|---|---|
| A | B |
```

- Figure caption immediately after the image, no blank line between them.
- Table and listing captions immediately before their block.
- Spaced separator ` - ` or ` – ` after the key; keys short, lowercase,
  unique per kind. Numbers are assigned at build time.
- A listing may be pulled from a file instead of pasted: `@listing md.py` on
  its own line under the caption, `@listing md.py:582-607` for a fragment.
  Path is relative to `listings_dir` (or `images_dir` when unset).

## References, citations, formulas

- Always by key: `[рис:pipeline]`, `[табл:req]`, `[лист:split]`,
  `[форм:count]`. Never hard-code a number.
- Citations `[1]`, `[1; 2]`, `[1-3]`; `[1, 2]` is not a GOST citation.
  Keyed style (`[{gruber}]`) is an alternative — do not mix the two.
- Escape literal brackets in prose: `\[note\]`, `\{key\}`.
- Display formula numbered by a key line directly under it:

  ```markdown
  \[ N = \sum_{i=1}^{k} 1 \]
  {count}
  ```

## Tables and lists

Pipe tables only; every body row must match the header's cell count (that is
an error, not a warning). `- `, `1)`, `а)` for lists, two-space indent for
nesting.

## Intentional findings

```markdown
<!-- @suppress unknown-reference -->
```

Silence by rule name, at the element it concerns; `<!-- @suppress-file … -->`
covers the rest of the file. A directive that silences nothing is reported as
a warning, so remove stale ones.

## Verify

`vkr-builder.bat lint` (Windows) or `./vkr-builder.sh lint`. Findings point
at `файл:строка` in the file you edited.
